@@ -3,3 +3,19 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+- Throws a `SyntaxError` if `pointer` is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3): it must be empty or start
+  with `/`, and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`.
+- Throws an `Error` if the pointer does not resolve (§4): missing member, out-of-range or malformed array
+  index (no leading zeros, no signs), the `-` token, or descending into a primitive or `null`.
+- Only own members resolve (`__proto__`, `constructor`, array `length` etc. do not, unless an own member).
+- The document is never mutated.
