+---
+id: task-001-implement-json-pointer-resolvepointer-rfc-6901
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Pointer resolvePointer (RFC 6901)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Request
+
+Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`: evaluate a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) against a
+JSON document and return the referenced value. Throw when the pointer is syntactically invalid (RFC 6901 §3)
+or does not resolve to a value of the document (§4).
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- "" refers to the whole document; "/" refers to the member with the empty-string name (§5 examples).
+- `~1` -> `/` and `~0` -> `~` unescaped in that order; any other `~` use is invalid (§3, §4).
+- Pointer not starting with "/" (and not empty) is invalid.
+- Array indices: `0` or digits without leading zeros; `-`, leading zeros, signs, non-digits do not resolve (§4).
+- Missing members, out-of-range indices and descending into primitives/null throw; a member whose value is `null` resolves to null.
+- Only own properties resolve (no `__proto__`, `constructor`, `toString`, array `length`); document is not mutated.
+- Tests cover the RFC 6901 §5 examples and the error paths.
